{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And I will set your sunstones.</b> There is no parallel for the word כדכד in all of Scripture, and it is a precious stone." "<b>And your windows.</b> From the root שמש, and they are in the windows — one places glass in them, and this is the custom of royal palaces." "<b>[And your gates].</b> And they are those that serve at the gate." "<b>Aglow.</b> A precious stone, and the alef is added, and it is from the root כי אש קדחה באפי (Deuteronomy 32:22)." "<b>For stones of delight.</b> That a person has desire for them — unlike all other stones, which are cast about with no desire for them."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 54, :notes {1 "The annotation [צ\"ל חלונות] is a Masoretic note correcting the Ketiv; I have translated the corrected form חלונות."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:33.998991031Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}